      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for handling this case - we should take all reasonable precautions to avoid closing sockets on a live app.\n\nThe way this is written though, we may wind up closing sockets on a UID which we were told is UNFROZEN.\n\nConsider the following series of events:\n\n1) handleFrozenUids() is called for FROZEN UID XYZ. It queues up a EVENT_UID_FROZEN_STATE_CHANGED event for the handler thread.\n\n2) EVENT_UID_FROZEN_STATE_CHANGED is processed in handler thread, we add UID XYZ to mPendingFrozenUids\n\n3) An EVENT_REPORT_NETWORK_ACTIVITY event is queued to the handler thread.\n\n4) handleFrozenUids() is called for UNFROZEN UID XYZ. It queues up a EVENT_UID_FROZEN_STATE_CHANGED for the handler thread.\n\n5) Handler thread runs EVENT_REPORT_NETWORK_ACTIVITY which closes sockets for all UIDS in mPendingFrozenUids. We now close sockets for the live app UID XYZ despite having been just told that it is no longer frozen.",
      "revId": "c4d1da75e775467503c95453cdadf0edbc85eceb",
